    {
      "title": "Trump launches racist diatribe against Abdul El-Sayed at Iowa rally",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/01/trump-iowa-rally",
      "description": "<p>President again took aim at progressive Senate candidate and lauded Haley Stevens for endorsing Mike Rogers</p><p>Donald Trump railed against Democratic US senate hopeful Abdul El-Sayed at a campaign event in Iowa Sunday, repeatedly referring to the Michigan progressive as a “jihadist”.</p><p>Trump’s comments aimed to influence a neck-and-neck race that will play an outsized role in determining which party controls the senate after Tuesday’s midterm elections.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/01/trump-iowa-rally\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-02T01:07:23"
    },
    {
      "title": "Democrat Haley Stevens endorses Abdul El-Sayed’s Republican rival Mike Rogers",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/01/abdul-el-sayed-haley-stevens-michigan-senate",
      "description": "<p>Endorsement was met with backlash from the party, condemning Stevens for her ‘betrayal’</p><p>Congresswoman Haley Stevens, who lost the Michigan Democratic Senate primary to Abdul El-Sayed, endorsed his Republican rival, Mike Rogers, in an extraordinary rebuke of her party’s nominee on the eve of the midterm elections.</p><p>Her endorsement came in a video posted to X after she attended an event with Rogers at the predominantly Black Perfecting church in Detroit on Sunday. Stevens’s endorsement was the culmination of an escalating feud between the former primary rivals – primarily over support for Israel – that has roiled one of the most fiercely contested Senate contests of the cycle.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/01/abdul-el-sayed-haley-stevens-michigan-senate\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-02T00:12:17"
    },
